Z||000000||grinthock||05-31-2001||10:52 PM||||Hey everyone need your advice....<P>While out tonight I think I fried my alternator, I put a stereo in about 3 weeks ago, and now my voltage needle is just BARLY above 13 when it used to cost up near the red line...  I think I have (or am frying) my alternator....<P>What replacements other than stock could I use that can handle it?  I am running one Clarion 800W Amp, and that's all....  NO Stiffener Cap... I am going to pu a stiffener in though, because that should help a bit...<P>IdeaS?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://grinthock.2y.net/pics/87gt/S_P000386.JPG">  <P>Home page: <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroworld.com<BR>Home</A>  of the fiero voting booth!<BR>Owner of 85 GT<BR>87 GT Silver<BR>1995 Ford Escort Wagoon POS||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||05-31-2001||10:57 PM||||I am suprised you didn't fry your battery...<BR>Normally, a 13.8 volt charge is plenty!<BR>You might want to double check the voltage with a volt meter to see if the one in the car is correct...<BR>crash...<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Hey everyone need your advice....<P>While out tonight I think I fried my alternator, I put a stereo in about 3 weeks ago, and now my voltage needle is just BARLY above 13 when it used to cost up near the red line...  I think I have (or am frying) my alternator....<P>What replacements other than stock could I use that can handle it?  I am running one Clarion 800W Amp, and that's all....  NO Stiffener Cap... I am going to pu a stiffener in though, because that should help a bit...<P>IdeaS?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||06-01-2001||12:57 PM||||Humm I must be in trouble then because my volts are way up there! close to 15 volts with the car running.<BR> <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Shows/carlisle/image001.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Shows/carlisle/image001.jpg</A> ||||reg||11
Z||000003||theogre||06-01-2001||01:20 PM||||take the car someplace and have the system tested. Never trust the dash gauge to be accurate. You can often get this test done free.<P>GM made stock alternators to over 100 amps. They are all interchangable. The diferances are internal. You can get aftermarket alternators to even higher capacity.||||reg||1
