Z||000007||poupas||06-04-2001||05:13 PM||||You say your voltage readings were up near the red, and now they are just above 13. Your alternator may be starting to go. My reading was just below the red, and then one day, it dropped to just above 13. I noticed it right away and now my battery is not being fully charged. I talked to my mechanic and he has a alternator tester, it should be just over 14v with the car running. Before you shrug it off you may want to test the alternator before your battery decides it has had enough and leaves you looking for a boost.||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||06-04-2001||05:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SPDFREK:<BR><B> going alittle fast? LOLOLOL<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just a weeee little bit I suppose  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>poupas<BR>The alt I have in my car is realitivly new say like under a year or so. BUT thats not to say it can't be bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
